CORE
SyncTest
--cp `../../../../scripts/format_classpath.sh . ../../../lib/java-models-library/target/core-models.jar ../../../lib/java-models-library/target/cprover-api.jar` --java-threading
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[java::SyncTest\.testNull:\(\)V\.null-pointer-exception\.1\] .*Null pointer check: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Without --throw-runtime-exceptions, synchronizing on a null monitor is reported
as a null-pointer-exception assertion failure, consistent with every other null
dereference check in the Java front-end (the check is added during
instrumentation, not during bytecode conversion).
